---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import ResponsiveImage from '../components/ResponsiveImage.astro';
import data from '../../../../kb/research/references/data/global-connections.json';
import regions from '../../../../kb/research/destinations/regions.json';
import town from '../../../../kb/research/collections/global-town-candidate.json';
import konarkStory from '../../../../kb/research/stories/narratives/konark.json';
const townPhoto=konarkStory.image;
const photo=regions.assets.mukteswar;
const sourceNumber=(id:string)=>data.sources.findIndex(s=>s.id===id)+1;
---
<Shell title="Global Connections" active="about" wide related={false}><div class="wrap connections">
<section class="hero connection-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Odisha and the world · Global Connections</p><h1>Rooted here.<br/><em>Reaching further.</em></h1><p class="lead">A city becomes closer when someone there knows your story.</p><p>Imagine a classroom discovering Odisha through a shared project. An artist finding a new audience. Two communities learning something useful from each other. This is where we begin exploring those possibilities.</p><a class="utk-button" href="#our-starting-point">Begin with Bhubaneswar ↓</a></div><figure class="hero-media"><ResponsiveImage src={photo.src} alt={photo.alt} width={photo.width} height={photo.height} fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>Mukteswar, Bhubaneswar · a place to share with the world.</figcaption></figure></section>
<nav class="section-links" aria-label="Global Connections sections"><a href="#our-starting-point">Bhubaneswar’s connections</a><a href="#india">Learn from Indian cities</a><a href="#possibilities">What could grow here</a><a href="#town-learning">A town learning idea</a><a href="#take-part">Take part</a></nav>
<section id="our-starting-point" class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">An existing bridge</p><h2>Bhubaneswar <span class="highlight">↔ Cupertino</span></h2></div><p class="section-intro">A formal city relationship, supported by a community organisation.</p></div><div class="connection-feature"><div><p class="eyebrow">Odisha, India</p><h3>Bhubaneswar</h3><p>Our starting point</p></div><span class="bridge" aria-hidden="true">↔</span><div><p class="eyebrow">California, United States</p><h3>Cupertino</h3><p>A documented sister city</p></div></div><div class="reading-pair"><div><h3>There is already a foundation.</h3><p>Cupertino’s official account records a memorandum signed in November 2012. It describes a community nonprofit—the Cupertino–Bhubaneswar Sister City Initiative—supporting cultural exchanges, student programmes and delegation visits. <a class="reference" href="#global-cupertino" aria-label="Source 1: Cupertino">[1]</a></p><p>Our opportunity is to understand this existing work, learn what its organisers need, and explore ways to contribute with their agreement.</p></div><aside class="evidence-note"><p class="eyebrow">Where we stand</p><p><strong>One formal relationship verified in this review.</strong> A 2017 report proposed a link with Bloemfontein, South Africa; we have not verified an executed agreement. It is a research lead, not a second confirmed partner. <a class="reference" href="#global-bloemfontein" aria-label="Source 3: Bloemfontein proposal">[3]</a></p><p>This is a starting inventory. A complete BMC register could establish further relationships.</p></aside></div></section>
<section id="india" class="section comparison"><p class="eyebrow">Six cities · different lessons</p><h2>What can Odisha <em class="highlight">learn from India?</em></h2><p class="lead">Look at the people and programmes behind the agreement.</p><p class="measure-note">This is a selective comparison, not a league table. Some sources list historical agreements; others describe one programme. Their counts cannot establish a national rank or how many partnerships are active today.</p><div class="city-grid">{data.cities.map(city=><article class:list={['city-card',{'home-city':city.city==='Bhubaneswar'}]}><p class="eyebrow">{city.extent}</p><h3>{city.city}</h3><p class="partners">{city.partners}</p><p>{city.evidence}</p><div class="lesson"><p class="eyebrow">A lesson for us</p><p>{city.lesson}</p></div><details class="city-detail"><summary>Evidence &amp; limits</summary><p>{city.limit}</p><p>{city.sources.map(id=><a class="reference" href={'#'+id} aria-label={'Read source '+sourceNumber(id)}>[{sourceNumber(id)}] </a>)}</p></details></article>)}</div><div class="interpretation"><h3>Our reading of the comparison</h3><p>Bhubaneswar has a smaller documented network than Mumbai and the Chennai examples examined here. But it already has a formal link and a community organisation to learn from. The useful next step is a current public record and a well-run collaboration—not a target for accumulating signatures.</p><p>For Odisha as a whole, we still need to research other cities. Missing information about Cuttack, Puri, Rourkela, Sambalpur or Berhampur does not mean they have no international connections.</p></div></section>
<section id="possibilities" class="section"><p class="eyebrow">Possibilities to develop together</p><h2>Let a connection <em class="highlight">become something useful.</em></h2><p class="section-intro">These are ideas for future collaborations. Partners, funding and programmes have not been announced.</p><div class="possibility-grid"><article><span class="number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3>Share a culture</h3><p>An exchange around Odia literature, dance, craft or food—with artists and communities shaping how their work is presented.</p></article><article><span class="number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3>Learn together</h3><p>A supervised student research project, a shared classroom or a jointly made story collection. Start with a useful question and credit everyone’s work.</p></article><article><span class="number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3>Learn how a city works</h3><p>Connect willing practitioners around heritage care, public spaces or hospitality skills. Agree on a small, practical output before organising an exchange.</p></article></div></section>
<section id="town-learning" class="section town-learning" aria-labelledby="town-title">
<p class="eyebrow">A proposal to explore · {town.pair}</p><h2 id="town-title">{town.title}</h2>
<div class="town-introduction"><figure><ResponsiveImage src={townPhoto.src} alt={townPhoto.alt} width={townPhoto.width} height={townPhoto.height} loading="lazy"/><figcaption>{townPhoto.short_caption}</figcaption></figure><div><p class="lead">{town.lead}</p><p>{town.context}</p><a class="utk-button utk-button--secondary" href={town.reading.href}>{town.reading.label} →</a></div></div>
<div class="town-comparison">{town.places.map((place,index)=><article><p class="eyebrow">{place.area}</p><h3>{place.name}</h3><p>{place.text} <a class="town-reference" href={'#'+place.source_id} aria-label={'Town comparison source '+(index+1)}>[{index+1}]</a></p></article>)}</div>
<p class="town-difference">{town.difference}</p><h3 class="town-output-title">What could we make together?</h3>
<div class="possibility-grid">{town.outputs.map(output=><article><h3>{output.title}</h3><p>{output.text}</p></article>)}</div>
</section>
<p class="section-intro">Curious about the maritime past behind these conversations? <a href="/stories/maritime-memory/">Follow a small boat into a wider world →</a></p>
<p class="section-intro">Thinking about a visit or tourism project? <a href="/opportunities/">Explore official guidance and cultural ideas for Odisha →</a></p>
<section id="take-part" class="invitation"><div><p class="eyebrow">A section today. Room to grow.</p><h2>Bring a connection.<br/><em class="highlight">Begin a conversation.</em></h2></div><div><p>For now, Global Connections is part of Project Odisha. We are documenting what exists and exploring what could come next. A dedicated initiative may grow from this work over time.</p><p>Know a documented city link, cultural organisation or university collaboration? Help us find its story and evidence.</p><a class="utk-button" href="/contribute/?page=%2Fglobal-connections%2F">Suggest a connection →</a><p class="submission-note">Submissions through GitHub Issues are public. Share public sources; leave out private contact details.</p></div></section>
<details class="utk-disclosure sources"><summary>Sources, photograph credit &amp; how we compare</summary><p>Research checked 3 October 2026. This page documents other organisations’ relationships; their inclusion does not imply a partnership with or endorsement of Project Odisha. Programme descriptions have not been independently audited.</p><p>The Mumbai figure counts Los Angeles plus 16 further names in the 2025 municipal yearbook. The Chennai and Hyderabad entries are documented minimum samples; Bengaluru and Pune are examples of organising models. There is no common activity period or complete all-India denominator.</p><p>Cupertino’s profile gives a 2012 designation and MoU; a council staff report concerns the earlier August 2011 proposal. These are distinct stages. We retain this date discrepancy rather than implying a single fully reconciled founding date.</p><p>Private organisations can help people collaborate. Formal city agreements belong to the relevant public authorities. This section announces neither a new municipal agreement nor an internship programme.</p><ol>{data.sources.map(source=><li id={source.id}><a href={source.resource}>{source.title}</a> · {source.publisher}. {source.capture_note}</li>)}</ol><p><a href={photo.source}>{photo.caption}</a> · <a href={photo.license_url}>{photo.license}</a>. {photo.changes}</p><h3>Town learning proposal</h3><p>Heritage comparison checked {town.checked_on}. The activity and outputs are proposals by Project Odisha; no exchange or town partnership is announced.</p><ol>{town.sources.map(source=><li id={source.id}><a href={source.resource}>{source.title}</a>. {source.note}</li>)}</ol><p>Konark photograph: <a href={townPhoto.source}>{townPhoto.title}</a> by {townPhoto.creator} · <a href={townPhoto.license_url}>{townPhoto.license}</a>. {townPhoto.changes}</p><p>Interpretation and programme ideas: Project Odisha, founded by Ahimanikya Satapathy. Suggestions remain subject to human and counterpart agreement.</p></details>
</div></Shell>
<style>
.town-learning{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.town-introduction{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:clamp(24px,4vw,64px);align-items:center;margin-top:32px}.town-introduction figure{margin:0}.town-introduction img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.town-introduction figcaption{font-size:14px;margin-top:10px}.town-comparison{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:clamp(24px,4vw,64px);margin-top:40px}.town-comparison h3{font-size:32px;margin:8px 0}.town-difference{max-width:75ch;border-left:3px solid var(--earth);padding-left:20px;margin-top:28px}.town-output-title{font-size:30px;margin-top:40px}.town-reference{font-size:13px;white-space:nowrap}.connections{padding-bottom:40px}.connection-hero{gap:clamp(28px,5vw,90px)}.connection-hero h1{font-size:clamp(48px,5.7vw,94px)}.connection-hero>div>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:44rem}.connection-hero .hero-media img{aspect-ratio:1.12;object-fit:cover}.section-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px 26px;border-block:1px solid var(--line);padding:16px 0}.section-links a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;font-size:15px;text-underline-offset:5px}.connections section[id]{scroll-margin-top:28px}.section-intro{max-width:42rem;font-size:18px;line-height:1.65}.connection-feature{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-around;gap:24px;background:var(--sea);color:var(--paper);padding:clamp(24px,4vw,60px);margin:28px 0 40px}.connection-feature h3,.connection-feature .eyebrow{color:var(--paper)}.connection-feature h3{font-size:clamp(30px,3vw,50px);margin-bottom:12px}.connection-feature p:last-child{margin:0}.bridge{font-size:48px;color:var(--paper)}.reading-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:clamp(28px,6vw,100px)}.reading-pair h3,.interpretation h3{font-size:30px}.evidence-note{border-left:3px solid var(--earth);padding-left:26px}.reference{font-size:13px;text-underline-offset:3px;white-space:nowrap}.comparison{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.measure-note{max-width:70ch;margin-bottom:34px}.city-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:24px}.city-card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:1px solid var(--line);padding:clamp(22px,2.4vw,38px);background:var(--light);min-width:0}.city-card h3{font-size:36px;margin:0 0 14px}.city-card>.eyebrow{min-height:42px}.home-city{border-top:4px solid var(--earth)}.partners{font-weight:600;color:var(--sea)}.lesson{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:20px;margin-top:auto}.lesson p:last-child{margin-bottom:20px}.city-detail summary{min-height:44px;cursor:pointer;font-size:14px;padding:10px 0}.city-detail p{font-size:14px}.interpretation{margin-top:40px;max-width:78ch}.possibility-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:clamp(24px,4vw,64px);margin-top:38px}.possibility-grid h3{font-size:30px}.number{font:italic 48px var(--serif);color:var(--earth);display:block;margin-bottom:16px}.submission-note{font-size:13px;margin-top:18px}.sources{margin:40px 0;font-size:14px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.sources li{margin-block:20px;scroll-margin-top:25px}.sources summary{padding:14px 0;min-height:44px;cursor:pointer}.connections h2{max-width:22ch}.connections p{line-height:1.7}
@media(max-width:1100px){.city-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:700px){.city-grid,.reading-pair,.possibility-grid,.town-introduction,.town-comparison{grid-template-columns:1fr}.city-card>.eyebrow{min-height:0}.connection-feature{flex-direction:column;text-align:center}.bridge{transform:rotate(90deg)}.connections .section{padding-block:45px}.connection-hero{padding-top:32px}.connection-feature h3{font-size:34px}.sources ol{padding-left:22px}}@media print{.city-grid{display:block}.city-card{break-inside:avoid;margin-bottom:16px}.section-links{display:none}}
</style>
<script>
for(const link of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('.reference'))link.addEventListener('click',()=>{const sources=document.querySelector<HTMLDetailsElement>('details.sources');if(sources)sources.open=true;});
</script>
